  "verbalization": "Mesoridazine is linked to Htr2c through a shared biological pathway involving phenothiazines, which are a class of antipsychotic agents. The evidence suggests that Mesoridazine, as a member of the phenothiazine family, binds to Htr2c, with the lowest common ancestor of Mesoridazine and its related compounds being the phenothiazine class. This implies a potential mechanism of action where the structural similarity of Mesoridazine to other phenothiazines, such as Trifluoperazine and Dimetotiazine, facilitates their interaction with Htr2c. The presence of a common ancestor in the phenothiazine class suggests a shared functional or biochemical role, possibly through similar binding properties or receptor interactions. The evidence also highlights the importance of phenothiazines in mediating the interaction between Mesoridazine and Htr2c, reinforcing the notion that the relationship is rooted in a broader pharmacological context.",
